<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mojmír I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 846</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mojmír I was the first known ruler of the Moravian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>, regarded as the founder of Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, ruling from about 830 to 846. Around 833 he drove the Slavic prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pribina">Pribina</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nitra">Nitra</a> and united the lands north of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into a single state centred on the Morava valley. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> deposed him in 846 and installed his nephew Rastislav.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mojmir-i.jpg" alt="Mojmír I" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Slowakische Nationalbank, National Bank of Slovakia (Preßburg)(Slovenská národná banka, Bratislava); Jozef Vlček (painters); Peter Zelizňák · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mojmir_kniieza_Velkomoravske.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
